This directory contains build scripts for Wine related packages.

Create log subdirectory for log write or check logs in $TMPDIR/korinf-log.

Using:
./wine-etersoft.sh [ SYSTEM ] [ PROJECTVERSION ] [options]


Using example:

Build for the system Fedora 11 in last:
./wine-etersoft.sh Fedora/11

Build for all system for last version:
./wine-etersoft.sh
the same:
./wine-etersoft.sh all last

Check for build result:
./wine-etersoft.sh -c

Install build requires:
./wine-etersoft.sh -i

Build for Ubuntu/8.10 distro for unstable:
./wine-etersoft.sh Ubuntu/8.10 unstable

Force build for Ubuntu/8.10 distro
./wine-etersoft.sh Ubuntu/8.10 -f

Bootstrap for Wine 7-11:

-b/-B builds and publishes all normal packages, including *-full. Only the
non-aggregate packages are installed in the build image. BOOTSTRAP_EXCLUDE
controls this installation subset without changing MAINFILES/EXTRAFILES.
No fake gecko, mono or winetricks packages are created. Per-component
dependency checks also defer *-full; the complete-set check below is required
to validate aggregate dependencies once all components are published.

Before building any component, existing *-full metapackages and recognised
legacy placeholders are removed from the build container. Real components
are retained. Removal is checked by rpm/dpkg and stops on dependency conflicts;
it never uses --nodeps or forced dependency removal.

After all real components have been published, verify the complete set:
    ../tools/check-wine-install x86_64/RockyLinux/8 11-unstable

This command installs the public Wine binary packages, including *-full, in
one transaction in a disposable container from the base image. It rejects
an image that already contains Wine and never saves the container. The check
is separate from bootstrap: it must run after all components are available.
It supports RPM and DEB packages, requires curl and epm in the base image,
and uses /var/ftp and https://download.etersoft.ru by default (--help for overrides).
